truth statement:

"Truth statements are universal standalone statements of truth, a statement can be read and understood as a single statement. They are not ambiguous in isolation, they are in plain, simple and clear language, with no jargon"

"Truth statements can be moved from record to record, or split out into adjacent records as the original records grows, however they can NEVER be changed during moves."

"Truth Statements can be a stated positive; what in the project must be true. Or stated negative; what in the project must be absent."

"Agents are forbidden to write truth statements, they stay sacred to the human"

"Truth statements are built up over time, the picture of the project forms progressively."

"These statements have altitude; a higher altitude lets the agent decide more of the meaning, but the human retains less control, a lower altitude places more of the burden on the human but they gain more control."
